{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Solid table with the columns and data that are unique to that table."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-app-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic App Table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Minimal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" setup."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Richer Users and Products tables sharing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hooks/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" and reusable components."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start With Shared Features and Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { createAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" become defaults for every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-app-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create App Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" through its column definitions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>,\n    cell: (info) => <i>{info.getValue()}</i>,\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create A Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create each table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The call site provides table-specific inputs such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" and reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"; shared features and defaults come from the hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const [data, setData] = createSignal<Array<Person>>([])\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render With The Normal Table APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTable"},{"type":"text","value":" table. This simple path does not require "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppTable"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppHeader"},{"type":"text","value":", or registered components."}]},{"type":"code","value":"return (\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n        {(headerGroup) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n              {(header) => (\n                <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n                </th>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n        {(row) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n              {(cell) => (\n                <td>\n                  <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n                </td>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" override defaults from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":". Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-reusable-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional: Reusable Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The richer composable-tables example also uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-registry-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Registry Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hooks/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from '../components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  createAppTable,\n  useTableContext,\n  useCellContext,\n  useHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returned-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returned Helpers"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Solid table with shared features, row models, defaults, and registered components."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates column helpers with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" and registered component types already bound."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTableContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current table inside registered table components."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCellContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current cell inside registered cell components."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeaderContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one column helper per row type. Since the helper is bound to the app setup, registered JSX components are available on cell and header contexts."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.TextCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.NumberCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.RowActionsCell />,\n  }),\n])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-table-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Table Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create each table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". You provide table-specific options like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":", and reactive data; the shared table infrastructure comes from the hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const [data, setData] = createSignal(makeData(1_000))\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  debugTable: true,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned table includes JSX wrappers. The example uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.AppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" with a selector to subscribe to the state slices used by the table UI."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<table.AppTable\n  selector={(state) => ({\n    pagination: state.pagination,\n    sorting: state.sorting,\n    columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n  })}\n>\n  {(state) => {\n    const sorting = () => state().sorting\n\n    return (\n      <div class=\"table-container\">\n        <table.TableToolbar title=\"Users Table\" onRefresh={refreshData} />\n\n        <table>\n          <thead>\n            <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n              {(headerGroup) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n                    {(h) => (\n                      <table.AppHeader header={h}>\n                        {(header) => (\n                          <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                            <header.FlexRender />\n                            <header.SortIndicator />\n                            <header.ColumnFilter />\n                          </th>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppHeader>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n              {(row) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n                    {(c) => (\n                      <table.AppCell cell={c}>\n                        {(cell) => (\n                          <td>\n                            <cell.FlexRender />\n                          </td>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppCell>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n\n        <table.PaginationControls />\n        <table.RowCount />\n      </div>\n    )\n  }}\n</table.AppTable>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reusing The Component Registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The example creates "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"personColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"productColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" from the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":", then creates both Users and Products tables with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". Each table keeps its own signals and columns, while the shared hook owns features, row models, row IDs, and component conventions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When To Use This Pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTable"},{"type":"text","value":" API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","text":"Start With Shared Features and Options","level":2},{"id":"create-app-columns","text":"Create App Columns","level":2},{"id":"create-a-table","text":"Create A Table","level":2},{"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","text":"Render With The Normal Table APIs","level":2},{"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","text":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table","level":2},{"id":"optional-reusable-components","text":"Optional: Reusable Components","level":2},{"id":"component-registry-setup","text":"Component Registry Setup","level":3},{"id":"returned-helpers","text":"Returned Helpers","level":3},{"id":"component-columns","text":"Component Columns","level":3},{"id":"component-table-rendering","text":"Component Table Rendering","level":3},{"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","text":"Reusing The Component Registry","level":3},{"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","text":"When To Use This Pattern","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Solid table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` setup.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/hooks/table.ts` and reusable components.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `createAppTable`.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { createAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `createAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```tsx\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>,\n    cell: (info) => <i>{info.getValue()}</i>,\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `createAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and reactive `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst [data, setData] = createSignal<Array<Person>>([])\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `createTable` table. This simple path does not require `AppTable`, `AppCell`, `AppHeader`, or registered components.\n\n```tsx\nreturn (\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n        {(headerGroup) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n              {(header) => (\n                <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n                </th>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n        {(row) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n              {(cell) => (\n                <td>\n                  <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n                </td>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n)\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `createAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in `src/hooks/table.ts`.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from '../components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  createAppTable,\n  useTableContext,\n  useCellContext,\n  useHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                  | Purpose                                                                                      |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createAppTable`        | Creates a Solid table with shared features, row models, defaults, and registered components. |\n| `createAppColumnHelper` | Creates column helpers with `TFeatures` and registered component types already bound.        |\n| `useTableContext`       | Reads the current table inside registered table components.                                  |\n| `useCellContext`        | Reads the current cell inside registered cell components.                                    |\n| `useHeaderContext`      | Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components.                         |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. Since the helper is bound to the app setup, registered JSX components are available on cell and header contexts.\n\n```tsx\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.TextCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.NumberCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.RowActionsCell />,\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCreate each table with `createAppTable`. You provide table-specific options like `key`, `columns`, and reactive data; the shared table infrastructure comes from the hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst [data, setData] = createSignal(makeData(1_000))\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  debugTable: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned table includes JSX wrappers. The example uses `table.AppTable` with a selector to subscribe to the state slices used by the table UI.\n\n```tsx\n<table.AppTable\n  selector={(state) => ({\n    pagination: state.pagination,\n    sorting: state.sorting,\n    columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n  })}\n>\n  {(state) => {\n    const sorting = () => state().sorting\n\n    return (\n      <div class=\"table-container\">\n        <table.TableToolbar title=\"Users Table\" onRefresh={refreshData} />\n\n        <table>\n          <thead>\n            <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n              {(headerGroup) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n                    {(h) => (\n                      <table.AppHeader header={h}>\n                        {(header) => (\n                          <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                            <header.FlexRender />\n                            <header.SortIndicator />\n                            <header.ColumnFilter />\n                          </th>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppHeader>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n              {(row) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n                    {(c) => (\n                      <table.AppCell cell={c}>\n                        {(cell) => (\n                          <td>\n                            <cell.FlexRender />\n                          </td>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppCell>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n\n        <table.PaginationControls />\n        <table.RowCount />\n      </div>\n    )\n  }}\n</table.AppTable>\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe example creates `personColumnHelper` and `productColumnHelper` from the same `createAppColumnHelper`, then creates both Users and Products tables with `createAppTable`. Each table keeps its own signals and columns, while the shared hook owns features, row models, row IDs, and component conventions.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `createTable` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Composable Tables (createTableHook) Guide\n---\n\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Solid table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` setup.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/hooks/table.ts` and reusable components.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `createAppTable`.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { createAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `createAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```tsx\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>,\n    cell: (info) => <i>{info.getValue()}</i>,\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `createAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and reactive `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst [data, setData] = createSignal<Array<Person>>([])\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `createTable` table. This simple path does not require `AppTable`, `AppCell`, `AppHeader`, or registered components.\n\n```tsx\nreturn (\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n        {(headerGroup) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n              {(header) => (\n                <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n                </th>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n        {(row) => (\n          <tr>\n            <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n              {(cell) => (\n                <td>\n                  <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n                </td>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tr>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n)\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `createAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in `src/hooks/table.ts`.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from '../components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  createAppTable,\n  useTableContext,\n  useCellContext,\n  useHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                  | Purpose                                                                                      |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createAppTable`        | Creates a Solid table with shared features, row models, defaults, and registered components. |\n| `createAppColumnHelper` | Creates column helpers with `TFeatures` and registered component types already bound.        |\n| `useTableContext`       | Reads the current table inside registered table components.                                  |\n| `useCellContext`        | Reads the current cell inside registered cell components.                                    |\n| `useHeaderContext`      | Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components.                         |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. Since the helper is bound to the app setup, registered JSX components are available on cell and header contexts.\n\n```tsx\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.TextCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.NumberCell />,\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => <cell.RowActionsCell />,\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCreate each table with `createAppTable`. You provide table-specific options like `key`, `columns`, and reactive data; the shared table infrastructure comes from the hook.\n\n```tsx\nconst [data, setData] = createSignal(makeData(1_000))\n\nconst table = createAppTable({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  debugTable: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned table includes JSX wrappers. The example uses `table.AppTable` with a selector to subscribe to the state slices used by the table UI.\n\n```tsx\n<table.AppTable\n  selector={(state) => ({\n    pagination: state.pagination,\n    sorting: state.sorting,\n    columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n  })}\n>\n  {(state) => {\n    const sorting = () => state().sorting\n\n    return (\n      <div class=\"table-container\">\n        <table.TableToolbar title=\"Users Table\" onRefresh={refreshData} />\n\n        <table>\n          <thead>\n            <For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n              {(headerGroup) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n                    {(h) => (\n                      <table.AppHeader header={h}>\n                        {(header) => (\n                          <th onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                            <header.FlexRender />\n                            <header.SortIndicator />\n                            <header.ColumnFilter />\n                          </th>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppHeader>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n              {(row) => (\n                <tr>\n                  <For each={row.getAllCells()}>\n                    {(c) => (\n                      <table.AppCell cell={c}>\n                        {(cell) => (\n                          <td>\n                            <cell.FlexRender />\n                          </td>\n                        )}\n                      </table.AppCell>\n                    )}\n                  </For>\n                </tr>\n              )}\n            </For>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n\n        <table.PaginationControls />\n        <table.RowCount />\n      </div>\n    )\n  }}\n</table.AppTable>\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe example creates `personColumnHelper` and `productColumnHelper` from the same `createAppColumnHelper`, then creates both Users and Products tables with `createAppTable`. Each table keeps its own signals and columns, while the shared hook owns features, row models, row IDs, and component conventions.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `createTable` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n"}
